    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720-a1">

                <pb facs="1306" n="1182" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1182"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    13.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Assim Pacha to Mr. Heap.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte, Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi></placeName>,<date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1881-05-15"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            15, 1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">(Gt. No. 62517, St. No. 6.)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: I have received
                    the note yon were pleased to address to me on the 5th of this month, No. 38,
                    relative to an attack on the Rev. Mr. Pierce and three of his employés, by a
                    band of brigands, in the neighborhood of Baghchejik.</p>
                <p>I hastened to communicate this note to the ministry of justice and to transmit to
                    the prefecture a categorical order to discover and arrest those guilty of the
                    act.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed>M. ASSIM.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
